===============================================================================
THIRD-PARTY CREDITS, SCIENTIFIC ACKNOWLEDGMENTS & ATTRIBUTIONS
===============================================================================

This project ("Fruitfly Chess") synthesizes original
gameplay systems, full-stack architecture, and 3D procedural animations developed
by ayuuXploits with foundational research data, scientific models, and open-source
engines. Full attribution and gratitude are extended to the following original creators:

1. NeuroMechFly Biomechanical Drosophila Model:
   - Authors: Victor Lobato-Ríos, Shravan Tata Ramalingasetty, Pembe Gizem Özdil,
     Jovana Arandelovic, Neval Iyer, Bernhard Schenck, Pavan Ramdya, et al.
   - Reference: "Neuromechfly, an adult Drosophila melanogaster model for biomechanics
     and neuroscience." Nature Methods, 19(5), 620-627 (2022).
   - Attribution: The 3D multi-segment prothoracic leg articulation (coxa, trochanter,
     femur spindle, high-arched knee condyles, tibial spurs, 5-part tarsus, and claws)
     and biological foreleg grooming kinematics are adapted from and inspired by the
     anatomical schematics and kinematic joint limits of the NeuroMechFly framework.

2. FlyWire Whole-Brain Drosophila Connectome:
   - Authors: Dorkenwald et al., Schlegel et al., FlyWire Consortium,
     Princeton University & MRC Laboratory of Molecular Biology (Cambridge).
   - Reference: "Neuronal wiring diagram of an adult brain." Nature (2024).
   - Attribution: The biological brain graph topology (256-node neuropil subgraphs,
     sensory projections, mushroom bodies, central complex, and motor control pathways)
     and synaptic weight distributions are structured based on the FlyWire whole-brain
     electron microscopy dataset (FAFB).

3. Stockfish Chess Engine:
   - Authors: The Stockfish Developers (https://stockfishchess.org).
   - License: GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPLv3).
   - Attribution: Tactical deep-search evaluation and NNUE positional heuristics are
     powered by Stockfish open-source engine technology.

4. Python-Chess:
   - Author: Niklas Fiekas (https://github.com/niklasf/python-chess).
   - License: GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPLv3).
   - Attribution: Board state management, legal move generation, and UCI/FEN parsing.

5. Three.js & React Three Fiber Ecosystem:
   - Authors: Ricardo Cabello (Mr.doob) and Poimandres (https://github.com/pmndrs).
   - License: MIT License.
   - Attribution: 3D WebGL rendering, scene graph management, and post-processing.
